Based on the discourse mentioned above in Hilchos Perikah u&rsquo;Te&rsquo;inah, Halacha 2, beginning &ldquo;Vay&rsquo;hi mikeitz &mdash; ki m&rsquo;rachamam y&rsquo;nahageim.&rdquo;

For the essential compassion is to illuminate the da&rsquo;as in the world &mdash; to know that Hashem is G-d, and to bring Israel out from their sins, which are a spirit of folly, etc. And even when [the tzaddikim] depart, the da&rsquo;as must remain in the world. And therefore, one needs to leave behind a son and a student, so that his da&rsquo;as remains below even when he ascends above. For when he is above alone, this is not completeness. The essential completeness is when one merits to be above and below, for both together are called a &ldquo;world.&rdquo;

And this is the aspect of a son and a student, for one needs to illuminate in the upper realms and in the lower realms, in the aspect of: &ldquo;For all is in the heavens and in the earth&rdquo; (I Divrei HaYamim 29:11), etc. And this is the aspect of a son and a student &mdash; see there. And through illuminating in a son and a student, one merits the aspect of makifim [surrounding lights], the aspect of: &ldquo;The ultimate purpose of knowledge is that we do not know&rdquo; &mdash; the aspect of the flow of the Keser &mdash; see there. And through the totality of son and student, one merits during eating to receive the illumination of the Ratzon [Will], the aspect of: &ldquo;At this time it shall be said to Yaakov and to Israel, &lsquo;What has G-d wrought?&rsquo;&rdquo; (Bamidbar 23:23), the aspect of: &ldquo;And You give them their food in its time&rdquo; (Tehillim 145:15). For the Malchus receives the parnasah from the Sea of Wisdom, which is drawn through the illumination of son and student, etc., etc. &mdash; see all this there well.

&sect;2

And this is the aspect of the inheritance that belongs to the children. For the essential money and parnasah is drawn from them &mdash; from the aspect of son and student. For through the totality of son and student, from there the Malchus receives the parnasah, as above. For each person must leave behind a blessing, that children remain from him in the world &mdash; that is, a son and a daughter, as our Sages of blessed memory said. And if not, G&ndash;d forbid, his soul remains naked, G&ndash;d forbid, as is brought in the Holy Zohar. For there is no completeness for the soul except when children remain from him in the world, as is well understood from the discourse mentioned above. For one needs to be above and below, as above &mdash; for this is why the soul descended into this world and clothed itself in this murky body.

And was it not better for the soul to be in the heights above, in the place where its tent was originally? But in truth, there is no completeness for the soul when it is above alone. The essential completeness is when it merits to bind the worlds together, the upper with the lower. And for this it clothed itself in a body &mdash; to bind the worlds. For body and soul are the aspect of the upper realms and the lower realms, the aspect of heaven and earth, as our Sages of blessed memory expounded (Sanhedrin 91a) on the verse: &ldquo;He calls to the heavens above&rdquo; (Tehillim 50:4) &mdash; this is the soul; &ldquo;and to the earth&rdquo; &mdash; this is the body.
